## Why This Is Asked

This question probes end-to-end coverage for real-time, multi-tenant architectures with RBAC, data isolation, and performance under load, mirroring production concerns in large-scale analytics platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time WebSocket testing at scale (1k streams)
- Strict per-tenant data isolation to prevent leakage
- Dynamic RBAC changes mid-session and their immediate effects
- Deterministic data seeds for repeatable tests
- Network throttling and latency percentile validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test outline (outline only)
async function testTenantDashboardScale() {
  await provisionTenant({ id: 'tenantA' });
  const wsPool = new WebSocketPool('/stream/tenantA', 1000);
  await wsPool.connectAll();
  // emit synthetic events, verify aggregates stay tenant-scoped
  await verifyIsolation('tenantA');
  await simulateRBACChangeMidSession('tenantA', 'viewer', 'editor');
  await verifyAccess('tenantA', 'editor');
  await throttleNetwork(1000);
  await verifyLatencyPercentile('tenantA', 95);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate no cross-tenant data leakage under peak load?  
- How would you parameterize scales (1k vs 5k) and ensure test determinism across runs?
